INT. ICE-MINING RIG CONTROL CAB - NIGHT

A cramped cab bolted to the side of a comet fragment. Frost on the windows. Red warning lights pulse.

ANSELM DRAKE (40s, miner, worn flight suit) straps into the operator seat. A radio crackles on the dash.

CONTROL (V.O.)
Rig Nine, this is Control. Report.

ANSELM
Rig Nine. Drill's jammed at four hundred meters.

CONTROL (V.O.)
Copy. Is the cable still tensioned?

ANSELM
Tensioned and shaking.

CONTROL (V.O.)
Anselm, you need to cut it loose.

ANSELM
If I cut it, I lose the whole string.

CONTROL (V.O.)
If you don't, you lose the rig.

Anselm checks a gauge. The needle is buried in the red.

ANSELM
How long have I got?

CONTROL (V.O.)
Eight minutes, maybe less.

ANSELM
Maybe less. Great.

CONTROL (V.O.)
Anselm. Listen to me.

ANSELM
I'm listening.

CONTROL (V.O.)
The fragment is rotating faster than predicted. The tether will snap.

ANSELM
Then tell me what to do.

CONTROL (V.O.)
Release the clamp.

ANSELM
That's what I'm trying to --

The cab lurches. A cup slides off the dash and shatters.

ANSELM (CONT'D)
It's not releasing!

CONTROL (V.O.)
Use the manual override.

He flips a cover. Pulls a lever. Nothing.

ANSELM
Manual's dead.

CONTROL (V.O.)
Then go outside.

ANSELM
Outside?

CONTROL (V.O.)
Hammer it free.

ANSELM
You want me to hit it with a hammer.

CONTROL (V.O.)
I want you to live.

Anselm grabs a helmet. Seals it.

ANSELM
Tell my sister I said --

CONTROL (V.O.) ^
Tell her yourself when you're back.

ANSELM ^
Tell her I said it was a good rig.

He slaps the airlock. It cycles open on black.
